    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0239" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.48/564½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Polish Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kwapiszewski</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="57" xml:id="d236-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>The Chargé d’Affaires ad interim of Poland presents his compliments to the
                    Secretary of State and, acting upon instructions of the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs, begs to advise that Dr. Ludwik Rajchman was relieved of the duties of
                    delegate in the United States of the Polish Government for matters of relief for
                    civilian population of Poland.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-07">January 7,
                            1941</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> No. 738/SZ–14. </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d236-f1" n="57" type="source" xml:id="d236-f1-content">
                <p>This note was handed to the Adviser on Political Affairs, James C. Dunn, by the
                    Polish Chargé with the remark that this matter had been the subject of
                    communications between the Polish Government and the American Chargé in London,
                    and not through the Polish Embassy in Washington.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
